page6+='\nTC 910 is active at the joint corner here, not at the two XOR-positive corners. Its current native C2 coefficient on g6 is **positive** (about +2.8). The other accepted terms cancel much of its joint-corner contribution. This is not a unique XOR feature or a causal explanation. [Full native terms](worked_cases/TC_910_native_terms.csv) and [nine-output accounting](worked_cases/TC_910_output_accounting.csv) retain the complete remainder.\n\n## Validation, preservation and scope\n\nExact controls, empty/rank-deficient/full-rank synthetic factorization, forward criterion priority, true-zero-change edge errors, decoder-independent API, bank completeness, every edge/corner ordering, locked ID alignment, canonical FP64/FP32 equality, matrix reload, Penrose/projector identities and both affine identities passed. Synthetic full-hidden-rank zero residual is algebraic sanity, not discovery. All six PNG/PDF figures were visually inspected with categorical entity labels. The original preservation audit verified **2,318** existing files unchanged, including checkpoints and M,d. Protected-final populations were never scored.\n\nExact calibration proves the stated four-point facts. The learned results support this frozen affine readout on the specified development domain. They do not establish output sufficiency, unique semantic coordinates, causal necessity, independent manipulability, global validity, or protected-final performance. Rejected cases are unsupported by this readout under this contract, not proof that every readout fails. No rescue refinement or further training was performed.\n'
